<Bindings>
	<!--
		M5a-i-D2. The client auto-loads a file literally named Bindings.xml from an addon's own
		folder: no line in Elmira_Vanilla.toc names it, and none should: adding one would load it a
		second time. This is Blizzard's own special binding format, not a generic Ui\ file, which is
		why it has no <Ui> wrapper.

		BINDING_HEADER_ELMIRA and BINDING_NAME_ELMIRA_CYCLE_ROTATION_MODE are plain string globals,
		set once at Core/Init.lua's file scope (the composition root); this is what the Key Bindings
		panel reads for the section header and this binding's own label, and there is no L[...] seam a
		file in this format can be routed through.

		Calls Elmira:CycleRotationMode() directly (Core/Init.lua) rather than naming a bare global
		function: `Elmira` is already the one WoW global this addon ever publishes, so the keybinding
		needs no second one just to be reachable from XML.
	-->
	<Binding name="ELMIRA_CYCLE_ROTATION_MODE" header="BINDING_HEADER_ELMIRA">
		Elmira:CycleRotationMode()
	</Binding>
</Bindings>
